**Shipped and verified the GPT-audited open-tracking safety set** (0.11.342–349): publish now rides the release CAS atomically; the open-at-NL dcache-reopen hole is closed fail-closed at `open()`; eager bit-clear at last close; B6 fails closed on unreadable bitmaps; recovery can no longer free without EX; icluster mounts are refused pending publish support.

**Built and verified the survivor sweep (C8)** through three successively-proven leak roots (dentry pinning, reload flag-stripping, stale cached nlink — each caught by the new `openunlink_deaths.sh` harness). Both crash arms now pass: **unlinker_death** (data intact through B's death, zombie swept, adopted-authority freed 6s after close) and **opener_death** (a dead opener's bits are now actually stripped — the purge's skip predicates had missed `open_holders` entirely — convergence in 93s).

